{"body":"The user requested that the active M5 KG-Microbe rebuild use updated MediaIngredientMech mappings, with a tracking issue and a review of the mapping file and changes before implementation.\n\nCurrent rebuild PR: #1750, head `3b07c58bb63776fdf1482dae34a8ca2212980620`.\n\n## Verified starting point\n\n- `mappings/mim_reviewed_release.json` pins MIM commit `1848b0fe521bc2462f165912fcf92d09ad9a8cec` and a reviewed export marked `2026-09-24`.\n- The actual `ingredient_mappings.sssom.tsv` consumed by MediaDive has SHA256 `6b52b30e018b369aa322d41dfd4e81fcfae0e895e34d7fe48900abf5835815fb`; the paired unified artifact has SHA256 `59464e08017cc907a1240a4378d2462efc9e2c1b9d6c3cf0b08b4344ef695ae8`. Fresh file hashes match producer finalization and completed 15-source admission evidence.\n- Current upstream MIM main is [`0dac278466699129a083343a921c2e0ca18a9ab4`](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/commit/0dac278466699129a083343a921c2e0ca18a9ab4), dated 2026-11-04. The newest change to the source SSSOM is [`b538ec76094e0d2d0667e5c3bd2455b24deceded`](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/commit/b538ec76094e0d2d0667e5c3bd2455b24deceded), also November 4. The latest tagged SSSOM release remains September 21, so a release-tag-only check misses later curation.\n- The existing graph merge is still running against the old mapping generation. Its inputs and evidence must remain immutable.\n\n## Review before implementation\n\n1. Freeze an exact current upstream candidate. First review the committed mapping changes and their scientific review chain read-only. Prepare candidate exports separately using the native supported/withheld workflow; do not install the raw source mapping table as if all rows were approved.\n2. Perform a separate read-only review of the resulting candidate artifacts against the consumed baseline: additions/removals, predicate/target changes, withdrawn approvals, alias suppression, owner/form changes, registry identities, exclusions and held rows. Bind findings to exact rows and evidence. Every finding becomes an issue and is triaged before implementation.\n3. Review the supported SSSOM and paired unified/registry artifacts together. Check KG-Microbe's current consumer policies, material/ingredient scopes and existing local corrections for stale assertions or conflicts. Preserve scientific holds and historical evidence; do not infer exact chemical identity or growth/absence from missing data.\n\n## Implementation and acceptance\n\n- After review and necessary repairs, update the immutable source/export pin and dependent artifacts coherently. Retain a compact machine-readable delta and review provenance, with helper scripts in the repository.\n- Use an isolated candidate/output generation; never mutate the inputs of the running merge or mix old and new receipts. Preserve the current run as comparison evidence. Determine affected producers from actual dependency bindings and rebuild/revalidate all invalidated outputs.\n- Run focused mapping/consumer checks and one real production-path canary before broader rebuilding. Verify saved graph outputs and admission receipts. Use the repository's single complete final gate on the final code candidate and required CI.\n- Validate the resulting canonical graph and archive, compare mapping-induced graph changes against the preserved baseline, and retain explicit MediaDive unknown-association qualifications.\n- Update PR #1750, or a clearly linked dependent PR if separation is necessary. No GitHub merge or release publication is authorized by this task.\n\nThis issue tracks use of current reviewed MIM mappings, not automatic acceptance of all current raw mapping rows. Review may identify dependent work in MIM; record it explicitly rather than weakening downstream admission.\n\n## Native workflow notes from independent read-only audit\n\n- `docs/MIM_REVIEWED_RELEASE.md` defines the mappings-only closure: ontologies_stubs, bacdive, mediadive, madin_etal, metatraits, metatraits_gtdb, bactotraits, gold and microbedecoder. Shared runtime/policy changes may require all 15 producers.\n- `scripts/refresh_reviewed_mim.py` reads the checkout's current pin and unified baseline and creates a new candidate directory. It has no alternate-pin or dry-run option. Use an isolated candidate worktree for proposed pin changes after the first review; do not mutate the running merge's checkout.\n- Pure read-only library validation exists in `scripts/mim_reviewed_release.py::validate_release`; immutable export binding is checked by `validate_immutable_export`. `audit_mim_historical_claims.py` writes a report and belongs to candidate preparation, followed by a separate read-only review pass.\n- Reconcile changes to the Python 3.13 export recipe, workflow, manifest, three reviewed products and review schema explicitly; never force new digests into outdated assumptions.\n- Preserve historical per-claim alias provenance, full-row quarantine multiplicity, identity-connected scope, hydrate direction and CAS controls. Replay all 55 documented historical MIM-derived MetaTraits overrides even though their table is excluded from candidate generation. Assess existing Potato, substrate, oatmeal and catalase safeguards against the actual candidate. Related issues #1318, #1317 and #1290 are context, not proof that a current repair is absent.\n","comments":[],"number":1788,"state":"OPEN","title":"Review and refresh MIM SSSOM mappings for the M5 rebuild","url":"https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/issues/1788"}
